{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-10972" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{6x-25}{x(x+5)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{(x+5)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, calculate $A+B.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-10972" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6x-25}{x(x+5)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{(x+5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $x(x+5)$ gives\n\n$$\n6x-25=A(x+5)+B(x).\n$$\n\nFor $x=0$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(0)-25 & =A(0+5)+B(0) \\\\ -25 & =5A \\\\ A & =-\\frac{25}{5} \\\\ A & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(-5)-25 & =A(-5+5)+B(-5) \\\\ -55 & =-5B \\\\ B & =\\frac{-55}{-5} \\\\ B & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA+B=-5+11=6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-10972" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9b32a3d6ebef79dd0ca7711e1ea66dbf1bb79bf3c2ffae90460b81de65d21987"} {"question" "q-10972" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-10972" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-10972" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-346796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{5{x}^{2}+10x-21}{(x-1)(x+2)(2x-3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{5{x}^{2}+10x-21}{(x-1)(x+2)(2x-3)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $-$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x-1$ |  | $x+2$ |  | $2x-3$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-346796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}+10x-21}{(x-1)(x+2)(2x-3)}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{B}{x+2}+\\frac{C}{2x-3}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-1)(x+2)(2x-3)$ gives\n\n$$\n5{x}^{2}+10x-21=A(x+2)(2x-3)+B(x-1)(2x-3)+C(x-1)(x+2).\n$$\n\nFor $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(1)^{2}+10(1)-21 & =A(1+2)(2(1)-3)+B(1-1)(2(1)-3)+C(1-1)(1+2) \\\\ -6 & =-3A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-2)^{2}+10(-2)-21 & =A(-2+2)(2(-2)-3)+B(-2-1)(2(-2)-3)+C(-2-1)(-2+2) \\\\ -21 & =21B \\\\ B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=\\frac{3}{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+10(\\frac{3}{2})-21 & =A(\\frac{3}{2}+2)(2(\\frac{3}{2})-3)+B(\\frac{3}{2}-1)(2(\\frac{3}{2})-3)+C(\\frac{3}{2}-1)(\\frac{3}{2}+2) \\\\ \\frac{21}{4} & =\\frac{7}{4}C \\\\ C & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}+10x-21}{(x-1)(x+2)(2x-3)}=\\frac{2}{x-1}-\\frac{1}{x+2}+\\frac{3}{2x-3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-346796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9b32a3d6ebef79dd0ca7711e1ea66dbf1bb79bf3c2ffae90460b81de65d21987"} {"question" "q-346796" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-346796" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-346796" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-346796" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-346796" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-346796" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-350930" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{3x+5}{(x-3)(2x+1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n|  | $\\frac{3x+5}{(x-3)(2x+1)}\\,=\\,\\frac{2}{x-3}\\,\\,+$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $2x+1$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-350930" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+5}{(x-3)(2x+1)}=\\frac{2}{x-3}+\\frac{B}{2x+1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-3)(2x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n3x+5=2(2x+1)+B(x-3).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-\\frac{1}{2})+5 & =2(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)+B(-\\frac{1}{2}-3) \\\\ \\frac{7}{2} & =-\\frac{7}{2}B \\\\ B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+5}{(x-3)(2x+1)}=\\frac{2}{x-3}+\\frac{-1}{2x+1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-350930" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9b32a3d6ebef79dd0ca7711e1ea66dbf1bb79bf3c2ffae90460b81de65d21987"} {"question" "q-350930" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-350930" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-350945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{3x+10}{(x+4)(x+5)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{3x+10}{(x+4)(x+5)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x+4$ |  | $x+5$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-350945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+10}{(x+4)(x+5)}=\\frac{A}{x+4}+\\frac{B}{x+5}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+4)(x+5)$ gives\n\n$$\n3x+10=A(x+5)+B(x+4).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-4$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-4)+10 & =A(-4+5)+B(-4+4) \\\\ -2 & =A \\\\ A & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-5)+10 & =A(-5+5)+B(-5+4) \\\\ -5 & =-B \\\\ B & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+10}{(x+4)(x+5)}=\\frac{-2}{x+4}+\\frac{5}{x+5}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-350945" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9b32a3d6ebef79dd0ca7711e1ea66dbf1bb79bf3c2ffae90460b81de65d21987"} {"question" "q-350945" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-350945" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-350945" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-350945" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-350988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{2}{(1-x)(2x-3)(x-2)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{2}{(1-x)(2x-3)(x-2)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} | $-$ | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $1-x$ |  | $2x-3$ |  | $x-2$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-350988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{(1-x)(2x-3)(x-2)}=\\frac{A}{1-x}+\\frac{B}{2x-3}+\\frac{C}{x-2}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(1-x)(2x-3)(x-2)$ gives\n\n$$\n2=A(2x-3)(x-2)+B(1-x)(x-2)+C(1-x)(2x-3).\n$$\n\nFor $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =A(2(1)-3)(1-2)+B(1-1)(1-2)+C(1-1)(2(1)-3) \\\\ 2 & =A \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=\\frac{3}{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =A(2(\\frac{3}{2})-3)(\\frac{3}{2}-2) \\\\  & \\,+B(1-\\frac{3}{2})(\\frac{3}{2}-2) \\\\  & \\,+C(1-\\frac{3}{2})(2(\\frac{3}{2})-3) \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{1}{4}B \\\\ B & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =A(2(2)-3)(2-2)+B(1-2)(2-2)+C(1-2)(2(2)-3) \\\\ 2 & =-C \\\\ C & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{(1-x)(2x-3)(x-2)}=\\frac{2}{1-x}+\\frac{8}{2x-3}-\\frac{2}{x-2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.json" "file_sha256" "2a991fc1816e1138b9b7ed1858cf682bdc83e7197ec10d3b10c3b2669c5d6e16"} {"question" "q-350988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9b32a3d6ebef79dd0ca7711e1ea66dbf1bb79bf3c2ffae90460b81de65d21987"} {"question" "q-350988" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008799/state.j